backfill for ZK 10.4 parity (2026-08-05) — see tasks/backfill-8-components-and-version.md
zul/css/norm.css.dsp is no longer purely the above commit's output: it gained the
20 --zk-severity-* tokens, compiled from ZK 10.4's own zul/less/profiles/_default.less
imported byte-identically. Every other file here is still that commit's output,
proven by the 1-changed/0-missing/0-extra manifest check taken across the update.

Also backfilled (same date): 8 component outputs that never existed in this theme —
js/zul/wgt/css/{avatar,avatargroup,badge,breadcrumb,carousel,chip,confirmpopup}.css.dsp
and js/zkmax/db/css/daterangebox.css.dsp. Their baseline is the zklessc output of ZK
10.4's own LESS, imported byte-identically, so for these 8 the LESS lane is the reference
just as it is for the other 77. NOTE: at the moment of import baseline and candidate come
from the SAME compile, so cssdiff's "0 differing" is true by construction and proves
nothing for them; the real comparison starts when they are converted to CSS.

backfill for ZK 11 parity (2026-08-13) — see tasks/zk11-jar-baseline-visual-ab.md
Upstream (origin/master) moved 6 commits past the fork commit above. Measured against
zk 11.0.0-jakarta.FL.20260811-Eval's own jars, exactly 3 outputs had drifted:
  js/zkmax/grid/css/grid.css.dsp   +.z-grid--stacking responsive card reflow (ZK-5409)
  js/zul/db/css/calendar.css.dsp   +.z-cell-range-* (Calendar.setRangeHighlight)
  zul/font/font-awesome.css.dsp    -.fas/.fass/.far/.fab bare aliases (upstream REMOVED)
All three are now the jar's bytes verbatim, extracted by scripts/jar-baseline.js.

Why the jar rather than a local zklessc run: the jar is built by ZK's own pipeline, so it
is an INDEPENDENT witness to the toolchain this branch is retiring. It earns that role by
measurement, not assertion — 78 of its 81 outputs were ALREADY byte-identical to this
baseline before the backfill, and those 3 were the entire difference. The two toolchains
agreeing on 78/78 of the untouched files is what licenses trusting it on the other 3.
Same caveat as 2026-08-05 applies to those 3: their baseline and the ZK 11 jar are now the
same bytes by construction, so `cssdiff jar baseline` reporting 0 proves nothing for them;
what it does prove is that no OTHER file drifted.
